Name: COMPASS_2014_I1278730
Year: 2014
Summary: Unpolarized charged-hadron cos(phi) and cos(2phi) SIDIS amplitudes
Experiment: COMPASS
Collider: CERN SPS fixed target
InspireID: 1278730
Status: UNVALIDATED
Reentrant: true
Authors:
 - Andreas Papaefstathiou <apapaefs@kennesaw.edu>
References:
 - Nucl.Phys.B 886 (2014) 1046-1077
 - arXiv:1401.6284
RunInfo: >
  Requires zero-polarization 160 GeV mu+ p and mu+ n samples, with POSNLO
  and NEGNLO generated separately. The LU sin(phi) observable is deliberately
  excluded because it requires the polarized beam sample.
NumEvents: 100000
NeedsCrossSection: yes
Beams: [[ANTIMUON, PROTON], [ANTIMUON, NEUTRON]]
Energies: [[160.0, 0.938272], [160.0, 0.939565]]
Description: >
  Stores 16 phi-bin yields, full-phi depolarization sums and event second
  moments in the published 1D and 3D charged-hadron bins. Postprocessing fits
  constant, cos(phi), cos(2phi) and a nuisance sin(phi), excluding the two
  bins adjacent to phi=0, then divides by the mean depolarization factor.
  The result is a stable-hadron generator diagnostic,
  not a detector-unfolded or controlled TMD/twist-3 prediction.
Keywords: [DIS, SIDIS, fixed-target, azimuthal asymmetry, charged hadron]
